From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 19:12:23 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] drivers/smmstore: Tell the code that set the memory up that
 the firmware booted

SMMSTORE_CMD_VBOOT_SLOT_GOOD is the payload saying that the firmware
booted. Besides the firmware watchdog of the platform
(smmstore_firmware_confirmed()), the code that set the memory up may
want to know: with an optional, faster memory profile, a firmware that
reaches the payload is what tells a profile that works from one that
only trains.

Add a second weak hook, smmstore_memory_confirmed(), called at the same
moment.

TEST=Build of the ThinkPad W541 with the native RAM init and of the
ThinkCentre M920x.

Change-Id: I44c968486f9d2caa9b0898c7bd0ed7e08e458cbb
---
 src/drivers/smmstore/smi.c | 12 +++++++++++-
 src/include/smmstore.h     |  1 +
 2 files changed, 12 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/drivers/smmstore/smi.c b/src/drivers/smmstore/smi.c
index 17f0bd84..411e46d9 100644
--- a/src/drivers/smmstore/smi.c
+++ b/src/drivers/smmstore/smi.c
@@ -290,6 +290,14 @@ static uint32_t vboot_try_other(void)
  */
 __weak void smmstore_firmware_confirmed(void) {}
 
+/*
+ * The same moment, for the code that set the memory up: the memory carried
+ * the firmware to the payload.
+ */
+__weak void smmstore_memory_confirmed(void)
+{
+}
+
 uint32_t smmstore_exec(uint8_t command, void *param)
 {
 	uint32_t ret = SMMSTORE_RET_FAILURE;
@@ -304,8 +312,10 @@ uint32_t smmstore_exec(uint8_t command, void *param)
 	 * watchdog needs neither to be stopped, and one left running would
 	 * reset the OS at every timeout.
 	 */
-	if (command == SMMSTORE_CMD_VBOOT_SLOT_GOOD)
+	if (command == SMMSTORE_CMD_VBOOT_SLOT_GOOD) {
 		smmstore_firmware_confirmed();
+		smmstore_memory_confirmed();
+	}
 
 	/* No parameters: coreboot sends it too, on S3 resume */
 	if (command == SMMSTORE_CMD_VBOOT_LOCK) {
diff --git a/src/include/smmstore.h b/src/include/smmstore.h
index 20391dfd..d3a19176 100644
--- a/src/include/smmstore.h
+++ b/src/include/smmstore.h
@@ -224,5 +224,6 @@ void lb_smmstorev2(struct lb_header *header);
  * payload, before the command itself can fail (weak)
  */
 void smmstore_firmware_confirmed(void);
+void smmstore_memory_confirmed(void);
 
 #endif
-- 
